  "technicalEffectsOfRefusal": "A completed refusal journal may add a private backup/tree and a recovery ref refs/git-layers/transactions/<UUID>/<layerId>. The strict oracle requires every preexisting ref unchanged, each added ref equal a PREEXISTING checkpoint OID, object type tree, and a matching completed rename-layer journal with the correct Layer identity. This is not a promise of universal zero writes.",
  "limitations": [
    "Current working Layer branch must be left before rename; its native staged data is preserved on refusal.",
    "Destination ref, config (including empty section) or reflog is occupied even if another component is absent. No force overwrite.",
    "Branch configuration outside the main local config, case/Unicode path aliases, ancestor-name changes, linked worktrees and non-files ref backend are conservatively unsupported. No global config or remote mutation is used to compensate.",
    "Interruption immediately after native branch copy but before its durable fingerprint snapshot preserves both refs, complete source history, config and backups, then recover refuses ambiguity with RECOVERY_CONFLICT. Manual inspection is required; no claim of universal interruption recovery.",
    "External divergent refs/config/reflogs and disputed Git locks are preserved. No ACID guarantee against raw concurrent writers, no exhaustive MODEL-008 or power-loss certification.",
    "A suíte npm completa executou os 16 casos juntos, mas a primeira seleção ampla terminou exit 1 e será reexecutada após correções de infraestrutura. Uma execução não substitui a outra."
  ],
